  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing  effectiveness, accessibility, sustainability and scale up of HIV treatment programs in the EECA region with special emphasis on key populations - World - Multicountry EECA ECUO (01-Nov-2015-31-Oct-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry EECA ECUO, HIV, ICO East Europe and Central Asia Union of People Living with HIV (ECUO)This program has the following goals: To enhance the effectiveness, accessibility, sustainability and scale up of HIV treatment programs in the Eastern Europe and Central Asia (EECA) region with special emphasis on key populations. The objectives of this program are: Advocate for transition to the strategic and sustainable state funding of the continuum of HIV care, based on evidence and on the needs of key populations, in five participating countries in the region.  Create enabling conditions at national and regional levels for facilitating access to HIV care and improving linkages between the main elements of the continuum of HIV care for key populations in five participating countries in the region</narrative>
  </description>
